> [OK][LA]HOM[A][ CITY][ -] Kevin[ Durant] scored 25 points[,] James[ Harden] added a spark with 23 points off the bench while[ returning] from[ an] injury and[ the] Oklahoma[ City] Thunder ended a string of futility against the[ Houston][ Rockets] with a[ 122]-[104] victory.
The Thunder got out to a sizz[ling][ start] and opened[ a] 23-point lead within the first 14 minutes. Their lead was never in jeopardy against a Houston team desperately needing a[ late][ charge][ to] make the playoffs.[
]Instead[,][ Oklahoma] City used its second[-]best shooting performance[ of][ the] season to take a big step toward solidifying its spot in the postseason.[
]Lu[is][ Sc]ola[ scored] 25 and Trevor Ariza added 20[ points] for Houston,[ which] fell seven[ games] behind Oklahoma City and 51/2 behind eighth-place Portland[ in] the Western Conference.[
]BOSTON - Paul[ Pierce] scored 27 points, Kevin Garnett had 20 and the Boston Celtics clin[ched] a playoff berth with a[ win][ over] the[ Denver][ Nuggets][.]
